Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:22:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] Pictures skipped while a video plays are
 told in kodi.log, and a stream set up again counts its start apart

The player information said "skipped 1" after the start of Avatar and
Carrie, 2 for Hokum, and 7 for Hokum after its output was switched
while it played, and kodi.log said nothing of any of them: neither the
choice that skipped them nor what came before it.

A picture is skipped where the one after it is due as well (late by
nearly a period or more, PrepareNextRender()). That has two causes:
the output showed no new picture for more than a refresh and a half
before the choice (a pass of the interface, a change of mode, a seek,
the render thread held up), or the pictures were already late when
they came (the decoder, the player). StartSkips.h, CSkipsTold: each
choice that counts pictures as skipped is told once, with how many
(and how many in the video), how late the picture shown instead was,
how long before it the picture before was chosen, in refresh periods,
and which of the two that says; ten a video, then one line that the
rest are counted only. Nothing is left out of the count.

A stream set up again while the video plays (its output chosen again
for the video, pictures of another format: CRenderManager::Configure()
after a picture of it was shown) shows no picture until the renderer is
set up, while the clock follows the sound that plays on: the pictures
that come due before its first frame are those of a start
(CStartSkips::Start(true)), counted apart and said as of the stream set
up again, as at the start of a video.
